            "review_title": "Review at Cinnamon Restaurant",
            "review_text": "uninspiredbea\nRutherford, Australia205 contributions\n0\nBeautiful setting, best pastries, but average hot food\nOct 2016 • Family\nWe only dined here for the buffet breakfast, which was included with our stay. Of the 5 hotels we stayed at while in Vietnam, Cinnamon was my least favourite as far as hot foods went, but most liked for their pastries. There wasn't much of a fruit selection either. Bonus for me was having condensed milk at the coffee/tea station. The restaurant itself is quite big, clean, new and modern. The service was nice and we appreciated that we were able to keep our son's frozen peas in their freezer.\nRead more\nService\nFood\nWritten October 30, 2016\nClimber659568\nDear uninspiredbea,\n\nWe would like to thank you for sharing your review. We're very glad you have enjoyed our homemade pastries, and will definitely work on improving our selection of hot breakfast food as well as fruit options. Hope to welcome you back soon and provide you with a more enjoyable experience.\n\nCinnamon restaurant\nRead more\nWritten November 1, 2016\nThis response is the subjective opinion of the management representative and not of Tripadvisor LLC nor of its partners.",
